#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:6
msgid "Colors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:11
msgid "Selecting Palettes and Default Colors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:19
msgid "**Track/Hotcue Palette**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:14
msgid ""
"It is possible to assign colors to tracks and :ref:`hotcues <interface-"
"hotcues>` to highlight them. Mixxx offers a selection of different palettes "
"that you can choose colors from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:18
msgid ""
"You can also make your own palette by clicking the :guilabel:`Edit` button "
"next to the palette name. This will open a the :ref:`palette editor "
"<configuration-colors-editor>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:25
msgid "**Default Hotcue Color**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:22
msgid ""
"It is possible to either select a single color from the current hotcue "
"palette that will be assigned to all newly created hotcue colors, or select "
"the :guilabel:`By hotcue number` option. The latter will automatically "
"assign a color from the palette to new hotcues based on the hotcue number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:30
msgid "Editing Palettes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:32
msgid ""
"The palette editor allows you add, modify, reorder and remove colors in a "
"color palette and save it under a new name. You can also delete custom "
"palettes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:35
msgid "To modify a color, double-click it to open the color picker window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:37
msgid ""
"When editing the hotcue palette, the palette editor also allows assigning a "
"specific default color to a hotcue number. This setting is honored when "
":guilabel:`Hotcue default color` is set to `By hotcue number`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:41
msgid ""
"That makes it possible to assign just a few distinct colors to your hotcues "
"automatically, but still have more colors available in the palette in case "
"you want to override the color manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:45
msgid ""
"For example, if you have a color palette consisting of 4 colors, and you "
"configure the palette to assign the first color to hotcue 1 and the third "
"color to hotcue 2, then hotcue 1 will use the first color and hotcue 2 will "
"be assigned the third color. The colors will repeat when setting a hotcue "
"with a number greater than those used in the palette. In the example above, "
"hotcue 3 will use the first color and hotcue 4 the second color, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:52
msgid ""
"You can also assign the same color to more than one hotcue. For example by "
"separating the hotcue numbers with a comma (“2, 4, 7”), expressing a range "
"of numbers (“1 - 3”) or any combination of that (“6, 1 - 3, 7”)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:56
msgid ""
"If no color in the palette has a hotcue number assigned to it, new hotcues "
"will use the color at the same index from the palette (i.e. hotcue 1 will be"
" assigned the first color in the palette, hotcue 2 uses the second color in "
"the palette, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:64
msgid "Replacing Hotcue Colors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:66
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's necessary to bulk replace colors of existing hotcues in your "
"library. Instead of changing the color of every single hotcue manually, you "
"can :guilabel:`Replace` to open the cue color replace dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapters/preferences/colors.rst:70
msgid ""
"In addition to selecting the new color, you may set conditions that "
"determine which hotcues the new color will be assigned to. If you tick both "
"checkboxes, the new color will only applied if both conditions match."
msgstr ""
